   "source": [
    "### Vectorization\n",
    "\n",
    "Vectorization is used to speed up the Python code without using **loop** structures. For instance, the dot product (inner product) between two vector: \n",
    "$$a_{1 \\times n} \\cdot b_{n\\times 1} = c$$\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 0,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {},
    "colab_type": "code",
    "id": "TTj-idSszrqf",
    "outputId": "2f43f606-b6e9-4bcf-bedd-07f51c51820f"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "dot_product = 203182.0\n",
      "Computation time = 9.644216999999955ms\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import time \n",
    "a = np.random.randint(10, size=10000)\n",
    "b = np.random.randint(10, size=10000)\n",
    "\n",
    "tic = time.process_time() \n",
    "dot = 0.0; \n",
    "  \n",
    "for i in range(len(a)): \n",
    "      dot += a[i] * b[i] \n",
    "\n",
    "toc = time.process_time() \n",
    "print(\"dot_product = \"+ str(dot)); \n",
    "print(\"Computation time = \" + str(1000*(toc - tic )) + \"ms\") "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "colab_type": "text",
    "id": "Vua8q7Auzrqn"
   },
   "source": [
    "Now, we can use the vectorized way"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 0,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {},
    "colab_type": "code",
    "id": "5s3NRadHzrqp",
    "outputId": "55247ba0-f4c8-450b-a3fa-157247af7526"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "n_dot_product = 203182\n",
      "Computation time = 0.3147210000000733ms\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "n_tic = time.process_time() \n",
    "n_dot_product = np.dot(a, b) \n",
    "n_toc = time.process_time() \n",
    "  \n",
    "print(\"\\nn_dot_product = \"+str(n_dot_product)) \n",
    "print(\"Computation time = \"+str(1000*(n_toc - n_tic ))+\"ms\") "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "colab_type": "text",
    "id": "NSomNs1Rzrqy"
   },
   "source": [
    "Another way, but with outer product (tensor product): \n",
    "$$a_{n\\times1}b^{T}_{1\\times n} = c_{n\\times n}$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 0,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {},
    "colab_type": "code",
    "id": "Z96WDyMjzrq0",
    "outputId": "9bae9b05-dae7-4df8-ee16-944e19bc7764"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "outer_product = [[27.  9.  3. ... 24.  6.  6.]\n",
      " [63. 21.  7. ... 56. 14. 14.]\n",
      " [63. 21.  7. ... 56. 14. 14.]\n",
      " ...\n",
      " [27.  9.  3. ... 24.  6.  6.]\n",
      " [63. 21.  7. ... 56. 14. 14.]\n",
      " [63. 21.  7. ... 56. 14. 14.]]\n",
      "Computation time = 60486.06629199999ms\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "tic = time.process_time() \n",
    "outer_product = np.zeros((10000, 10000)) \n",
    "  \n",
    "for i in range(len(a)): \n",
    "    for j in range(len(b)): \n",
    "        outer_product[i][j]= a[i]*b[j] \n",
    "\n",
    "toc = time.process_time() \n",
    "print(\"outer_product = \"+ str(outer_product)); \n",
    "print(\"Computation time = \"+str(1000*(toc - tic ))+\"ms\") "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "colab_type": "text",
